<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1400" height="980" viewBox="0 0 1400 980">
  <defs>
    <style>
      .bg { fill: #0b1020; }
      .panel { fill: #111a33; stroke: #2a3a6a; stroke-width: 2; rx: 18; }
      .box { fill: #0f1730; stroke: #3a57a6; stroke-width: 2; rx: 14; }
      .box2 { fill: #0e1a2e; stroke: #3aa67a; stroke-width: 2; rx: 14; }
      .box3 { fill: #15122a; stroke: #a67a3a; stroke-width: 2; rx: 14; }
      .hdr { font: 700 26px/1.2 Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial; fill: #e7ecff; }
      .subhdr { font: 700 18px/1.2 Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial; fill: #cfe0ff; }
      .txt { font: 15px/1.35 Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial; fill: #d6dcff; }
      .mono { font: 14px/1.35 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace; fill: #d6dcff; }
      .muted { fill: #9fb0e6; }
      .tiny { font: 12px/1.3 Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial; fill: #a7b4e8; }
      .arrow { stroke: #8fb3ff; stroke-width: 3; fill: none; marker-end: url(#arrowHead); }
      .arrow2 { stroke: #57e6b0; stroke-width: 3; fill: none; marker-end: url(#arrowHead2); }
      .arrow3 { stroke: #ffbf78; stroke-width: 3; fill: none; marker-end: url(#arrowHead3); }
      .badge { fill: #1c2b55; stroke: #3a57a6; stroke-width: 2; rx: 10; }
      .callout { fill: #0c142d; stroke: #6b84d6; stroke-width: 2; rx: 12; }
    </style>

    <marker id="arrowHead" markerWidth="12" markerHeight="12" refX="10" refY="6" orient="auto">
      <path d="M0,0 L12,6 L0,12 Z" fill="#8fb3ff"/>
    </marker>
    <marker id="arrowHead2" markerWidth="12" markerHeight="12" refX="10" refY="6" orient="auto">
      <path d="M0,0 L12,6 L0,12 Z" fill="#57e6b0"/>
    </marker>
    <marker id="arrowHead3" markerWidth="12" markerHeight="12" refX="10" refY="6" orient="auto">
      <path d="M0,0 L12,6 L0,12 Z" fill="#ffbf78"/>
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <rect class="bg" x="0" y="0" width="1400" height="980"/>

  <text class="hdr" x="60" y="58">Supervised Learning Warmup (Teacher-Forcing) — What Happens Per Training Sample</text>
  <text class="txt muted" x="60" y="86">Goal: learn to generate the correct structured “next step” given graph state + previous context.</text>

  <rect class="panel" x="50" y="110" width="1300" height="820"/>

  <g transform="translate(80,150)">
    <rect class="badge" x="0" y="0" width="220" height="46"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="16" y="30">Inputs (from dataset)</text>

    <rect class="box" x="0" y="70" width="560" height="150"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="18" y="98">1) Graph + Step-Pair</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="124">nodes: precomputed text embeddings for each node</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="146">edges: connectivity between nodes</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="168">step_pair: previous → next transition</text>
    <text class="tiny" x="18" y="196">Source: PenTestDataset.__getitem__ builds prompt_text + target_text + full_text</text>

    <rect class="box" x="0" y="240" width="560" height="190"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="18" y="268">2) Prompt and Target Text</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="296">prompt_text = "[GRAPH]\\nPrevious Context...\\nGenerate Next Step..."</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="322">target_text =</text>
    <text class="mono" x="36" y="346">Strategy: ...</text>
    <text class="mono" x="36" y="370">Step: ...</text>
    <text class="mono" x="36" y="394">MCP Tasks: ...</text>
    <text class="tiny" x="18" y="418">Warmup uses teacher-forcing: model sees gold target tokens during training</text>
  </g>

  <g transform="translate(720,150)">
    <rect class="badge" x="0" y="0" width="250" height="46"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="16" y="30">Core Computation</text>

    <rect class="box2" x="0" y="70" width="600" height="170"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="18" y="98">3) Build Conditioning Vector (the “policy_out”)</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="124">A) Encode previous_text with SentenceTransformer → previous_emb</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="146">B) Encode graph (nodes + edges) with GNN → graph_emb</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="168">C) Fuse: combine([graph_emb, project(previous_emb)]) → policy_out</text>
    <text class="tiny" x="18" y="194">policy_out has size = LLM hidden size; one vector per sample</text>

    <rect class="box2" x="0" y="260" width="600" height="190"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="18" y="288">4) Tokenize Full Sequence and Inject Graph</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="314">tokenized_full = tokenizer(prompt_text + target_text)</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="336">inputs_embeds = Embedding(tokenized_full.input_ids)</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="358">Replace first token embedding:</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="382">inputs_embeds[:, 0, :] = policy_out</text>
    <text class="tiny" x="18" y="408">This makes the LLM “see the graph” via the special [GRAPH] token position</text>
  </g>

  <g transform="translate(80,520)">
    <rect class="badge" x="0" y="0" width="300" height="46"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="16" y="30">Loss Construction</text>

    <rect class="box3" x="0" y="70" width="560" height="210"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="18" y="98">5) Teacher-Forcing Labels (mask the prompt)</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="124">Compute prompt length separately:</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="148">prompt_token_len = tokenizer(prompt_text).input_ids.shape[1]</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="176">Create labels = full input_ids, then ignore prompt tokens:</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="200">labels = input_ids.clone()</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="224">labels[:, :prompt_token_len] = -100</text>
    <text class="tiny" x="18" y="252">-100 tells Hugging Face loss to ignore those positions</text>
    <text class="tiny" x="18" y="270">So the loss is only on the target continuation (Strategy/Step/MCP Tasks output)</text>
  </g>

  <g transform="translate(720,520)">
    <rect class="badge" x="0" y="0" width="280" height="46"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="16" y="30">Optimization Step</text>

    <rect class="box" x="0" y="70" width="600" height="210"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="18" y="98">6) Forward → Loss → Backprop</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="124">Forward pass (mixed precision):</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="148">outputs = llm(inputs_embeds=..., attention_mask=..., labels=labels)</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="176">Loss is standard next-token cross-entropy over target tokens.</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="198">Then:</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="222">scaler.scale(loss).backward()</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="246">clip_grad_norm_(policy + llm, max_grad_norm)</text>

    <rect class="box" x="0" y="300" width="600" height="170"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="18" y="328">7) Update Weights</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="356">scaler.step(optimizer)</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="380">scaler.update()</text>
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="404">scheduler.step()</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="432">Both the policy (GNN+project/combiner) and the LLM weights get updated.</text>
  </g>

  <path class="arrow" d="M640 250 C700 250, 700 250, 720 250"/>
  <path class="arrow2" d="M640 360 C700 360, 700 360, 720 360"/>
  <path class="arrow3" d="M640 650 C700 650, 700 650, 720 650"/>

  <g transform="translate(80,820)">
    <rect class="callout" x="0" y="0" width="1240" height="90"/>
    <text class="subhdr" x="18" y="30">Key Intuition (easy mental model)</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="56">Warmup teaches the model “when you see this graph+context, the correct continuation is these labeled lines.”</text>
    <text class="txt" x="18" y="78">Graph info enters only via the first token embedding; loss ignores prompt tokens and trains only the generated answer region.</text>
  </g>
</svg>